  "answer_markdown": "The maximum number of web pages MistralAI-User may visit for a single user request in Vibe is not explicitly stated in the provided sources. The sources do not mention a specific limit for the number of web pages that can be visited in a single user request.\n\nRegarding the per-minute rate limit, sources [2], [3], [8], and [13] discuss rate limits, but they are related to API requests, tokens, or overall usage rather than the number of web pages visited per user request. These rate limits apply at the Workspace or organization level and are shared across all API keys in the Workspace.\n\nSources [4] and [6] mention limitations related to web search and Open URL functionality, but they do not specify a per-minute rate limit for visiting web pages.\n\n**Insufficient evidence**: The sources do not provide enough information to answer the question about the maximum number of web pages MistralAI-User may visit for a single user request or a specific per-minute rate limit for this functionality.",
