message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "To hand off your work from the terminal to a cloud session in Vibe Code Web, use the `/teleport` command inside an active local session. This moves the session to the cloud, preserving its history and branch state. The command is one-way, meaning you cannot move the session back to the local CLI once it has been teleported to the cloud.\n\nFenced code block with the relevant command:\n\n```text\n/teleport\n```\n\nBy using Vibe Code Web, you give up local filesystem access and local secrets, and you must ensure that the GitHub repository has been authorized for Vibe Code Web access. The cloud session runs on Mistral Medium 3.5 and follows GitHub branch protections, required reviews, `CODEOWNERS`, and required status checks, but it cannot bypass these rules or access repositories you have not authorized [8, 10, 11].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 8,
      "quote": "Teleport is part of the Vibe Code Web sandbox flow, currently in Public Preview. Capabilities, limits, and the interface can change before general availability."
    },
    {
      "n": 10,
      "quote": "Teleport is one-way. Once a session moves to the cloud, you can't pull it back into the local CLI. Continue from Vibe Code Web."
    },
    {
      "n": 11,
      "quote": "Vibe Code Web cannot: Access your local machine or local filesystem. Read or modify repositories you have not authorized. Bypass branch protections, required reviews, `CODEOWNERS`, or required status checks."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

