parsed.answer_markdown:
For the endpoint `POST /v1/chat/classifications`, the required fields in the `ChatClassificationRequest` body are:

1. **`model`** (string, required) — ID of the model to use.
2. **`input`** (object, required) — Chat to classify. It can be one of two types:
   - An `InstructRequest` object containing a required `messages` array (array of objects, required).
   - An array of `InstructRequest` objects.

```
{
  "model": "model-id-here",
  "input": {
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Hello, world!"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Or as an array:

```
{
  "model": "model-id-here",
  "input": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "role": "user",
          "content": "Hello, world!"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

- The `metadata` field is optional and can be an object or `null` [3].

